{"tool_name":"maude","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"maude","identifiers":[],"license":"custom, see /usr/share/doc/maude/copyright","summary":"High-performance logical framework","home_url":"http://maude.cs.uiuc.edu","keywords":[],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"maude","home":"https://github.com/Carldeboer/MAUDE","license":"MIT","summary":"Inferring expression changes in sorting-based CRISPR screens.\n\nMAUDE: Mean Alterations Using Discrete Expression.\n\nMAUDE is an R package for finding differences in means of normally distributed (or nearly so) data, via measuring abundances in discrete bins.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:26:35Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-20T17:20:30Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:maude","credit":[{"email":"carl.deboer@ubc.ca","name":"Carl G. de Boer","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8935-5921","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"aregev@broadinstitute.org","name":"Aviv Regev","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Read binning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3798"},{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"MAUDE","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S13059-020-02046-8","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s).Improved methods are needed to model CRISPR screen data for interrogation of genetic elements that alter reporter gene expression readout. We create MAUDE (Mean Alterations Using Discrete Expression) for quantifying the impact of guide RNAs on a target gene's expression in a pooled, sorting-based expression screen. MAUDE quantifies guide-level effects by modeling the distribution of cells across sorting expression bins. It then combines guides to estimate the statistical significance and effect size of ta